From: Gyuyoung Kim <qkim@google.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:39:39 -0800
Subject: [M150-LTS] Retain SVGImage across
 SVGImageForContainer::CreateViewInfo

SVGImageForContainer::CreateViewInfo() allocates Oilpan objects when
parsing SVG fragment view specifiers. An Oilpan allocation can
synchronously trigger sweeping and finalizers that cancel a shared
ImageResource and clear ImageResourceContent::image_. Callers that held
an unowned Image* or Image& across CreateViewInfo() could therefore
access a freed SVGImage afterward.

Hold a scoped_refptr<Image> across CreateViewInfo() in
HTMLImageElement::DefaultDestinationSize(),
ImageElementBase::ElementSize(), LayoutImageResource,
StyleFetchedImage, WebElement, and EventHandler, and store a
scoped_refptr<SVGImage> in SVGImageForContainer so that container
wrappers keep the underlying SVGImage alive.

NO_IFTTT=This CL is to cherry-pick the patch to the M150 branch.

(cherry picked from commit ae76c84a47e410f556dc10aa925e057216872cc4)

